# shelf: kneemri-members-3
# out: members_3
#
# comp/members3.roster — the THIRD weights dataset, `kneemri-members-3`, mounted beside the other two.
#
# WHY A THIRD PACKAGE EXISTS, and it is the SAME reason the second one does. `comp/members2.roster`
# states it: adding one member to a shelf means re-pushing the whole shelf, so "every member trained
# after the last big push was an offline gain that could never become a board gain." Shelf 1 has since
# grown to 156 members and ~13.8 GB, and shelf 2 to 41 members and ~3.6 GB — so shelf 2 now has the
# disease it was created to cure. A member costs 89 MB. Putting one on shelf 1 to ship it taxes the
# submission 13.8 GB; putting it here taxes it 89 MB.
#
# THIS IS A ROTATING SHELF, NOT AN ARCHIVE. When it grows past a gigabyte or so it stops being cheap
# and the next new member opens shelf 4 rather than paying this one's push. Nothing needs to move
# between shelves for that: `MemberPackage.spanning` merges every mounted root into one package, so
# which shelf a member sits on is a fact about what it cost to upload and about nothing else.
#
# NO MEMBER MAY APPEAR ON TWO SHELVES. `MemberPackage.spanning` REFUSES an identifier two roots both
# hold — "a duplicate is not a merge conflict, it is a vote loading weights nobody chose". Both members
# below were appended to `comp/members.roster` on 2026-09-20 and were moved here the same day, before
# either was packaged or pushed; that file now carries a pointer where they were.
#
# A KERNEL MUST DECLARE THIS SHELF to see anything on it: `dimiturnt/kneemri-members-3` in
# `dataset_sources`, beside the other two. A kernel that names a member from here without mounting it
# does not fail loudly — `KernelRun` DROPS a member it cannot mount and keeps going, which is the
# silent-drop failure `run_check` exists for. Run it on the kernel log before the slot is spent.
#
# A MEMBER FITTED ON ANY FOREIGN CORPUS CARRIES `# licence: <corpus>` ON ITS OWN LINE, exactly as on the
# other two shelves — `submit_check` refuses on the TAG's PRESENCE, so an untagged foreign member ships
# silently. Neither member below is foreign: both descend from `labelwise_ext_drop40_long_ema_s2026`,
# fitted on our own corpus.

basinsoup_k3_s2026.pt       # 0.8712 midpoint / 0.9089 ledger75. Three seed-children re-annealed off the
                            # fine-tuned parent labelwise_ext_drop40_long_ema_s2026 (0.9073) and averaged
                            # in weight space — the shared-basin condition the two earlier souping closes
                            # named as their only re-open (knee-0dfys). The best soup this project owns
                            # and +0.0016 over its own parent, one forward pass. Seats as a TWIN of
                            # labelwise_ext_drop40_long_s2026: swapping it in reads +0.0012, real but
                            # under the +0.0040 this ruler picks board ticks at, so hold it, never a slot.
                            # It is fold 0, so it trained on two thirds of the corpus while every solo
                            # this project has shipped is `--fold -1` — a board reading of it prices the
                            # soup and that fold penalty TOGETHER and can separate neither.
basinsoup_k4_s2026.pt       # 0.8709 midpoint / 0.9089 ledger75. The same average with the parent itself
                            # as a fourth member. It reads IDENTICAL to k3 to four decimals, which is the
                            # measurement that the children never left the parent's point — seat it only
                            # as k3's alternate, never beside it.
basinsoup_ff_k4_s2026.pt    # DARK, fold -1: no offline number exists or can be made. The same K=4 uniform
                            # weight average as the row above, moved onto the FULL-DATA line: parent
                            # labelwise_ext_drop40_long_ff (`extffsolo_v1`, board 0.945, the best solo this
                            # project owns) plus three 4-epoch seed-children forked off it at backbone-lr
                            # 2e-5, seeds 301/302/303. On the fold-0 line that operation read +0.0016
                            # ledger75 (0.9073 -> 0.9089), the only weight-space op this project has
                            # measured positive. Shipped as a solo; the board is its only ruler.
basinsoup_dmlb_k4_s2026.pt  # 0.8720 midpoint / 0.9092 ledger75, epoch 1, 909 rows — the HIGHEST fold-0
                            # number this project owns. Uniform weight average of `dml_b_s2026` (0.9078,
                            # the best honest fold-0 fit) and three 4-epoch seed-children forked off it at
                            # backbone-lr 2e-5, seeds 401/402/403. +0.0014 over the parent, against the
                            # same operation's +0.0016 on `basinsoup`'s base: the soup op REPRODUCES on a
                            # second base, and on a non-EMA parent. Under the solo board-transfer fit
                            # (knee-0dfys: slope +1.071, intercept -0.0307) this projects to board ~0.9436,
                            # so it is a shelf member and a base for further work, not a slot candidate.
basinsoup_ff_k3_s2026.pt    # DARK, fold -1: no offline number exists or can be made. The K=3 uniform
                            # weight average of the SAME three seed-children basinsoup_ff_k4 holds, with
                            # the parent anchor dropped -- the one-variable counterpart to the entry that
                            # boarded 0.946. Packaged as the instrument that attributes that +0.001 to
                            # the children's average or to the anchor, a question no offline ruler can
                            # answer on a full-data fit.
basinsoup_dmlb_ff.pt        # DARK, fold -1: no offline number exists or can be made. The _ff operation
                            # applied to a SOUP -- the order this project had never run. The champion
                            # `basinsoup_ff_k4_s2026` is soup-of-ff (children refitted whole-corpus, then
                            # averaged); this is ff-of-soup, four epochs at backbone-lr 2e-5 with
                            # --init-scope all on --fold -1 off `basinsoup_dmlb_k4_s2026`, whose 0.9092
                            # ledger75 is the highest fold-0 number this project owns. Pickable only
                            # after slot 56407707 measured the FOLD PENALTY at 0.002, which made a
                            # fold-0 number board-predictive at a -0.002 offset. Transfer puts the base
                            # at fit 0.9430; the refit term across four bases is +0.001/+0.003/+0.004/
                            # +0.007, so this projects to ~0.947 against a 0.946 champion. knee-17la8.
